{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1777387558,"nonce":"MoUTvf/YZ11dcM3tlz1YY4gTTDY=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABAu0T7M8AAAAFz02oxA"},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777415888,"nonce":"uMsFIQwcpoBZB/UlYo2OmiCQBCg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAqjNRw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/97#issuecomment-4339584327"},"message":"## Scope expansion — operator-action topics in the bag recorder\n\nThe salmon-side `/diagnostics` recorder (action #2 in the issue) should also capture the operator-originated *commands sent to the boat*. Without these, post-incident reconstruction can see \"boat did X\" via the boat-side bag but not \"operator told it to do X\" — and during a comms degradation event, the question is often whether commands were even sent vs sent-but-not-delivered.\n\nThese topics are published locally on salmon and forwarded to the boat via `udp_bridge` (per `bizzyboat_project11/config/operator.yaml:18-23,30-35`), so the recorder picks them up without any bridge dependency:\n\n- **`/bizzy/marine/command`** — CAMP-issued commands (mission control, mode changes, task triggers)\n- **`/bizzy/piloting_mode/manual/helm`** — manual joystick helm output\n\nAnything else operator-originated worth adding while we're at it (suggestions welcome — e.g., any future CAMP→boat topics, or operator-side `cmd_vel` if joystick output gets restructured) should be enumerated by reading `operator.yaml`'s `udp_bridge` topics list, since that's the canonical \"what the operator sends\" inventory.\n\n### Updated acceptance for action #2\n\n- [ ] Salmon-side recorder captures `/diagnostics`\n- [ ] Salmon-side recorder captures `/bizzy/marine/command`\n- [ ] Salmon-side recorder captures `/bizzy/piloting_mode/manual/helm`\n- [ ] (Optional) capture `/rosout`, `/tf` if cheap — useful for full op-side state\n- [ ] Verify post-deployment: bag contains both diagnostic time-series and command time-series, sufficient to answer \"during the wedge window, what did the operator send and what did the operator's monitors see?\"\n\n### Why this matters for the masquerade-removal investigation\n\nThe 2026-04-27 deployment ended with a partial network failure that we couldn't root-cause (`docs/logs/2026/2026-04-27_dev_logs.md § \"Recovery: many cycles, root cause indeterminate\"`). One hypothesis is that disabling masquerade on the operator router (2026-04-14, see `ccomjhc_project11/documentation/bizzyboat_network_debug_2026-04-14.md`) changed the failure surface for new TCP/UDP flows under sustained load. Op-side diagnostic + command bags would let us correlate (a) when commands stopped reaching the boat, (b) when op-side network monitors registered degradation, and (c) when boat-side bags show the boat stopped receiving — pinning the failure to a specific path with timestamps instead of \"things were broken for ~30 min.\"\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1777475615,"nonce":"evh5ZV0MjNJEtYPV8mOsvbw+/OY=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABAu0T7M8AAAAF0eoPHA"},"status":2}]}